statement:
The pinned source Situation \ref{situation-olsson-laszlo} (sites-cohomology.tex:5686–5704) consists of a site $\mathcal C$, a sheaf of rings $\mathcal O$, a **weak Serre** subcategory $\mathcal A\subset\mathrm{Mod}(\mathcal O)$, and a set $\mathcal B\subseteq\mathrm{Ob}(\mathcal C)$ covering all site objects, such that for each $V\in\mathcal B$ there is $d_V$ and cofinal coverings $\mathrm{Cov}_V$ for which $H^p(V_i,\mathcal F)=0$ for all $p>d_V$, all members $V_i$ of selected covers and every $\mathcal F\in\mathcal A$. The subcategory $D_{\mathcal A}(\mathcal O)$ comprises objects whose cohomology sheaves lie in $\mathcal A$. The conclusion is the completion of **any unbounded object with cohomology in $\mathcal A$** under the homotopy inverse limit of its standard lower truncations. The statement explicitly inherits the hypotheses of the named Situation; they are materialized here, not assumed for later unrelated lemmas.

